# The position y * w + x and the operand of (a * b) | 0 are doubles by type, and code generation computes them in integers: a sum of integers and one product of two is rounded only beyond 2^52. Two products, and a factor that may hold a fraction, stay doubles
# FORM: AsRead
# OPTIONS: heat=EverythingIsHot disable=pass:InlineCalls
# RUN: generate-code calls ExactIntegersBehindNumbers
# Where the target converts a number to an int32 in one instruction (ARM64 with FEAT_JSCVT) there is no call to see.
# RUN(CALLS): generate-code calls
# REQUIRES(CALLS): x86_64

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
variable g0 name="cells" module=m0 declared={type=anything} initialization=Undefined
function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="input" [isFreeName]
    v2 = ToNumber v1
    v3 = Integer integer=0
    v4 = BitOr v2, v3
    v5 = NewArray v4, v4, v4
    PutModuleVariable v5 variable=g0
    v7 = CallDirect v4, v4 function=f1
    v8 = CallDirect v4, v2 function=f2
    v9 = CallDirect v4, v4, v4, v4 function=f3
    v10 = CallDirect v4, v4, v4 function=f4
    v11 = CallDirect v4, v4, v4, v4 function=f5
    v12 = Add v7, v8
    v13 = Add v12, v9
    v14 = Add v13, v10
    v15 = Add v14, v11
    Return v15
}
function f1 name="lowWordOfProduct" parameters=[{type=i32}, {type=i32}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: i32, v1: i32):
    v2 = Mul v0, v1
    v3 = Integer integer=0
    v4 = BitOr v2, v3
    Return v4
}
function f2 name="lowWordOfProductWithNumber" parameters=[{type=i32}, {type=number}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: i32, v1: number):
    v2 = Mul v0, v1
    v3 = Integer integer=0
    v4 = BitOr v2, v3
    Return v4
}
function f3 name="lowWordOfTwoProducts" parameters=[{type=i32}, {type=i32}, {type=i32}, {type=i32}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: i32, v1: i32, v2: i32, v3: i32):
    v4 = Mul v0, v1
    v5 = Mul v2, v3
    v6 = Sub v4, v5
    v7 = Integer integer=0
    v8 = BitOr v6, v7
    Return v8
}
function f4 name="elementAtProductAndTerm" parameters=[{type=i32}, {type=i32}, {type=i32}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: i32, v1: i32, v2: i32):
    v3 = GetModuleVariable variable=g0
    v4 = Mul v0, v1
    v5 = Add v4, v2
    v6 = ElemGet v3, v5
    Return v6
}
function f5 name="elementAtTwoProducts" parameters=[{type=i32}, {type=i32}, {type=i32}, {type=i32}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: i32, v1: i32, v2: i32, v3: i32):
    v4 = GetModuleVariable variable=g0
    v5 = Mul v0, v1
    v6 = Mul v2, v3
    v7 = Sub v5, v6
    v8 = ElemGet v4, v7
    Return v8
}
# CHECK-LABEL: f1:
# CHECK-NOT: operationAOTToInt32
# CHECK-LABEL: f2:
# CALLS-LABEL: f2:
# CALLS: operation operationAOTToInt32 x1
# CALLS-LABEL: f3:
# CALLS: operation operationAOTToInt32 x1
# One in f1 and three in f4, where the test that the element is there and the read on either side of it each take the position. None in f5.
# CHECK: statistic ExactIntegersBehindNumbers 4
